    "body": "## Summary\n\nCloses #27.\n\n- Moves provider credential fields, archive imports, and direct probes into the Connections provider detail pages.\n- Keeps data sections lightweight: their empty-state guides now show a compact CTA into Connections instead of repeating setup cards inline.\n- Preserves `#conn-{provider}` deep links, now opening the matching provider detail inside Connections.\n- Keeps Settings as an app-level page with a single Open Connections action.\n- Adds the issue 27 case study with raw GitHub artifacts, online research, verification logs, and screenshots.\n\n## Screenshot\n\n![Connections Telegram detail](https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/blob/issue-27-05348a151c4d/docs/case-studies/issue-27/screenshots/final-connections-telegram-detail.png?raw=true)\n\n## Verification\n\n- [x] `npm test`\n- [x] `npm run lint`\n- [x] `npm run format:check`\n- [x] `npm run check:duplication`\n- [x] `npm run build:web`\n- [x] `RUN_BROWSER_E2E=1 npm run test:e2e:browser`\n- [x] Playwright MCP smoke test of Connections -> Telegram detail at desktop and mobile widths\n\n## Notes\n\n- Release prep: `.changeset/issue-27-connections-dry.md` marks this as a patch change.\n- Case study: `docs/case-studies/issue-27/` contains the requirement trace, solution plan, research notes, local verification logs, and preserved issue screenshots.\n",
